From: Zone Launcher
Subject: [PATCH] Smooth window, fullscreen and resolution changes; Alt+Enter/F11

Switching resolution or window mode, or the window manager resizing the
window (maximizing, tiling, dragging an edge), left the game at the wrong
size, with stretched or cropped menus and a misaligned mouse:

- After a device reset the OpenGL viewport kept the old size: GL keeps it
  across a reset and the main menu draws without setting one. Set it in
  CHW::Reset.
- The GL surface size came from the chosen resolution (vid_mode), not the
  window, so borderless fullscreen and window-manager sizes rendered at
  the wrong size until a second reset. CHW::GetSurfaceSize now returns the
  window's size in pixels.
- Every size event reset the renderer, and the reset set the window back
  to vid_mode, fighting the window manager (a tiling one keeps resizing).
  The renderer now follows the window's size once it has stayed the same
  for 250 ms, with one reset and without touching the window; a size the
  window manager picks is kept for the session and doesn't change
  vid_mode.
- UpdateWindowProps changed the size before leaving fullscreen (ignored
  by window managers), and did not wait for asynchronous changes
  (Wayland), causing extra resets at intermediate sizes. It now leaves
  fullscreen first, waits for the window to settle, maximizes a window as
  big as the screen, and leaves exclusive fullscreen before borderless.
  After leaving fullscreen it always sets the window size: SDL 3 reports
  a requested size before the compositor applies it, and the compositor
  restores the pre-fullscreen size otherwise.
- The UI's cursor scale is now recomputed when the window size changes,
  not only the render size; ImGui gets the window size.
- Focus changes un-maximized the window (SDL_RestoreWindow on activate)
  and minimized borderless fullscreen on focus loss; now only a minimized
  window is restored and only exclusive fullscreen is minimized.
- CRenderTarget left the per-context sizes of all but the immediate
  context uninitialized.

Alt+Enter and F11 switch between fullscreen and a window (through
vid_window_mode, so the choice is saved). The game doesn't see those keys.

---
